  "question": {
    "statement": "Consider a spherical shell of radius $R$ at temperature $T$. The black body radiation inside it can be considered as an ideal gas of photons with internal energy per unit volume $u = \\frac{U}{V} \\propto T^{4}$ and pressure $p = \\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\frac{U}{V}\\right)$. If the shell now undergoes an adiabatic expansion the relation between $T$ and $R$ is:",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "A",
        "text": "$T \\propto \\frac{1}{R}$"
      },
      {
        "id": "B",
        "text": "$T \\propto \\frac{1}{R^{3}}$"
      },
      {
        "id": "C",
        "text": "$T \\propto e^{-R}$"
      },
      {
        "id": "D",
        "text": "$T \\propto e^{-3R}$"
      }
    ],
    "source_claimed_answer": "A",
    "verified_answer": "A",
    "source_solution": null,
    "answer": "A",
